ABSENT_SIDES = tuple(one["absent"] for one in LANGUAGES)

# The inventory table an element names its text in, per language. It is derived
# from LANGUAGES rather than written out again, and deliberately: `english` and
# `latin` name the two sides of ONE fact --- which text, and if it is missing,
# why --- so the block a text arrives in and the side its absence is recorded on
# cannot be given different names and drift apart. One name per language and no
# more: a general `texts = [...]` array keyed by arbitrary language would invite
# a third language that the two-sided `absent` table above has no reason to
# offer for, and an element could then carry words nothing could say the absence
